CHAPTER IV

AUTHORITY, OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 7

1. The Regional Government has the authority and responsibility for the Protection of Women and Children victims of violence.
2. The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) include:a. guaranteeing the rights of women and children without discrimination in accordance with laws and regulations;
b. implementing policies for the protection of Women and Children victims of violence based on laws and regulations;
c. establishing policies, programs and activities for the protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
e. allocating budget in the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
g. improving the quality and competence of human resources who provide services/assistance for victims of violence against women and children; h. cooperating with the community and/or community organizations in the implementation of protection of women in accordance with laws and regulations;
i. taking preventive action in order to prevent violations of the rights of women and children.
3. The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to protect women and children as referred to in Article 7 paragraph (1) shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

REGENT OF KATINGAN,

Considering Recalling:
a. that with the enactment of Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection as amended by Law Number 35 Year 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 24 Year 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence, it is deemed necessary to prevent and overcome violence against Women and Children through legal protection for Women and Children victims of violence;
b. that based on the consideration as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children victims of violence;

: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 5 Year 2002 concerning Establishment of Katingan Regency, Seruyan Regency, Sukamara Regency, Lamandau Regency, Gunung Mas Regency, Pulang Pisau Regency, Murung Raya Regency and East Barito Regency in Central Kalimantan Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 18, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4180);
3. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
4. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 100, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 Year 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 Year 2016 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);
5. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 21 Year 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
7. Law Number 12 Year 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 13 Year 2022 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 12 Year 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 143, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6801);
8. Law Number 16 Year 2011 concerning Legal Aid (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 104, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5246);
9. Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 Year 2022 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 238, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6841);
10. Law Number 12 Year 2022 concerning Criminal Act of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
11. Government Regulation Number 4 Year 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 Year 2008 concerning Implementation of Women's Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 Year 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Child Protection;

